A kitchen island can completely change the way a kitchen looks and functions, but is a kitchen island worth it in a small London kitchen? The answer depends on the room's proportions, layout and how you actually use the space. While islands can provide extra worktop, storage and seating, forcing one into a compact kitchen can make the room feel cramped rather than practical. Consulting specialists in <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/kitchen-renovation-company/">bespoke kitchen design and renovation London</a> helps evaluate spatial clearances before committing to structural changes.

For London homes where space is often limited, the key is to make every part of the island work hard.
<h2>What Should You Consider Before Adding a Kitchen Island?</h2>
