<h3>How much space do you need around an island?</h3>
The first thing to consider is the clearance around the island. You need enough room to move comfortably between the island, worktops and appliances.

An island that leaves very narrow walkways may look impressive in a plan but become frustrating in everyday use. Doors, drawers and appliances also need enough space to open without hitting the island.

This is why an island should be planned as part of the overall kitchen layout rather than added simply because there is an empty section of floor. Leveraging <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/3d-render-services/">photorealistic 3D kitchen render visualization</a> lets you test circulation paths and sightlines before building begins.
<h3>What can a small kitchen island actually provide?</h3>
