Even a compact island can offer useful additional storage and preparation space. It could include drawers for everyday items, cupboards for larger appliances or a simple overhang for one or two stools.

The important thing is choosing features that suit the way you use your kitchen. If storage is your biggest problem, prioritise <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/bespoke-joinery-design-london/">custom kitchen cabinetry and bespoke joinery</a> tailored to millimeter accuracy. If you enjoy cooking, additional preparation space may be more valuable.

