<h3>Could a peninsula work better than an island?</h3>
Sometimes the answer isn't an island at all.

A peninsula can provide many of the same benefits while remaining connected to a wall or run of cabinetry. This can be particularly useful in narrow kitchens where a freestanding island would restrict movement.

It can also help create a subtle division between the kitchen and an adjoining dining or living area without completely closing the space off. In projects like our <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/barnet-residence-interior-design/">Barnet family residence kitchen transformation</a>, a peninsula arrangement preserved generous floor space while establishing a natural social divide.
