<h3>Should the island include seating?</h3>
If you regularly have breakfast in the kitchen or want somewhere for guests to sit while you cook, a small seating area can make the island much more useful.

However, you don't necessarily need a large breakfast bar. One or two carefully positioned stools may be enough. When planning your investment, researching an <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/open-plan-kitchen-renovation-cost/">open plan kitchen renovation cost</a> can help establish where to allocate budget between seating, quartz surfaces, and integrated appliances.
<h3>What should you consider when choosing the island's design?</h3>
The island should feel connected to the rest of the kitchen. Materials, cabinetry and worktops can be coordinated with the wider scheme, while lighting can help make it a visual focal point.

